# ⚙️ NetWatch Unified Mini-SOC — Complete Installation Guide

This guide covers setting up, running, and publishing your containerized NetWatch Mini-SOC on Ubuntu Server or homelab VM using Docker Compose.

Step 1: Clone or Create Your Project Directory
On your server, create your project folder and move into it:
mkdir netwatch-soc && cd netwatch-soc
mkdir static

Step 2: Configure Environment Variables (Optional)
If you want to customize your local server IP or map target coordinates:
cp .env.example .env
nano .env

Step 3: Build and Launch the Stack
Run Docker Compose to build the container images and start all services in the background:
docker compose up --build -d

Step 4: Verify Running Containers
Check that your services are up and running properly:
docker compose ps

Step 5: Access the Dashboard
Open your web browser and navigate to:
http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:3000

Step 6: Firewall & Port Reference
- NetWatch Web UI (Port 3000 TCP)
- Cowrie Honeypot (Ports 2222, 2223 TCP)
- Dionaea Honeypot (Ports 445, 21 TCP)

Recommended UFW Firewall Rules (Ubuntu)
sudo ufw allow from 192.168.0.0/16 to any port 3000 proto tcp comment 'Allow NetWatch UI on LAN only'
sudo ufw allow 2222/tcp comment 'Allow Cowrie SSH trap'
sudo ufw allow 445/tcp comment 'Allow Dionaea SMB trap'
sudo ufw enable
